WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.720
[ Music ]

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.039
[Narrator:] The Public Health Service, its
people and programs affect the lives of millions

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.660
of Americans every day.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.940
Whether it's a matter of medical research,
pure food and drugs,

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:41.200
contagious diseases, or the delivery of healthcare, the Public Health Service plays a significant role.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.940
How the Public Health Service became what
it is today is really the story of public

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.000
health in America.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.530
A story that is still unfolding.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.060
Throughout the years, the Public Health Service
has fought its battle in plague-ridden cities

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.660
and in the corridors of power in Washington.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:22.400
Today's Public Health Service agencies are
challenged by an ever-changing world, and they respond.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.460
The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention
strive to protect citizens from infectious

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.360
and non-infectious diseases.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.900
The Health Resources and Services Administration
supports the training of health professionals

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.080
and sends them to underserved areas.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.040
The National Institutes of Health conduct
basic research on diseases such as AIDS.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.460
The Food and Drug Administration hastens the
approval process to bring new drugs to the public.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.050
The Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services
Administration provide services for mental,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.720
behavioral, and addictive disorders.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.560
The health-related concerns connected with
hazardous waste are increasingly important

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.460
and are the responsibility of the Agency for Toxic Substances and Disease
Registry.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:19.260
A relatively recent addition to the PHS is
the Agency for Healthcare Policy and Research.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.560
The Agency strives to assess the effectiveness
of medical care.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.540
The Public Health Service also responds to
needy members of the community, providing

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.580
care to Native Americans through its Indian Health Service.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:38.800
It also assists the elderly, drug addicts,
those with AIDS, and others who might be forgotten.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.180
When it started, its mission then as well
was to serve a group that had little access

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.940
to medical care, merchant seamen.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:56.280
That was in 1798 when an Act of Congress,
signed into law by President John Adams,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.500
provided for the government to maintain hospitals

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:04.120
for sick or disabled seamen as had traditionally been done in England.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:13.560
[ Whistling and Music ]

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:17.840
For its first 80 years or so, what was then
known as the Marine Hospital Fund,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.720
was administered by customs inspectors in
the seaports of the new nation.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.980
As the United States grew, so did the number
of ports.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:32.720
Marine hospitals and clinics sprouted on the
East Coast as well as the West Coast

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.240
and up the Mississippi,

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.700
anywhere there was a waterway in the growing
nation.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.820
By 1870, the system needed to be revamped.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.160
The reorganization led to the appointment
of the first Surgeon General, John Maynard Woodworth.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.080
He had been an Army medical officer in the
Civil War.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.520
Woodworth put his officers in uniform, created
a flag, and instituted the military system

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.480
of appointment by merit.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:06.220
Dr. Woodworth's reforms were formalized by
law in 1889, when the Commissioned Corps of

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.760
the U.S. Marine Hospital Service was created.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.780
As the Commissioned Corps was expanding during
the closing years of the 19th century,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.120
so was biological discovery.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.480
The scientific ferment brought changes to
the Marine Hospital Service.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:28.600
It's Hygienic Laboratory, started in 1887,
was a pioneer in biomedical research.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.860
It manufactured biologicals and trained scientists

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.480
from state health departments in the  techniques of producing them.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:43.600
Years later, it became the National Institutes
of Health, the heart of American medical research.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.040
In the latter part of the 19th century, the
Marine Hospital Service was given another major responsibility,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:58.460
boarding vessels arriving at U.S. ports to
check passengers and crews for infectious diseases.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.320
This task had originally been handled by the
states, but as immigration mushroomed,

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.500
the responsibility was transferred to the
federal government.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.120
At all ports of entry, the Marine Hospital
Service was in charge of inspection of arriving immigrants,

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.620
including the most important of them of all,
Ellis Island.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.820
The Service pioneered the line.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.420
It was an efficient way to check for immigrants
with disease,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:30.440
blindness, and mental deficiencies, anyone
who might become a public charge.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:38.300
More than 12 million immigrants, as many as
5,000 a day at times, passed through Ellis Island.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:42.740
under the examining hands and watchful eyes
of the Marine Hospital Service.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.040
In 1902, the service was renamed.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.920
It became the Public Health and Marine Hospital
Service.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:58.710
In 1912, as legislation increased its scope
of activities, its name was simplified to

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.200
the Public Health Service.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:07.080
In the early 1900s, the Service led the fight
in investigating dozens of diseases

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.780
and developing treatments for them.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:15.680
The service battled trachoma, a serious, contagious
eye disease that can cause blindness.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.300
Commissioned Corps doctor John McMullen took
his team to the rural hills and hollows of Kentucky.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.580
He established a hospital and 11 field clinics.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:34.900
McMullen and his team taught personal hygiene
to local residents to stem the spread of the inflammation.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:40.300
Within 10 years, the incidence of trachoma
cases was drastically reduced.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:47.400
The PHS marshalled its energies in Montana's
Bitterroot Valley to combat Rocky  Spotted Fever.Mountain

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.000
The disease was carried by ticks on livestock
and other animals.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.440
PHS doctor Thomas McClintick, was sent to
Montana to find a way to control the disease.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:04.200
As he searched for a cure he became infected
with the disease and died.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:10.200
Dr. McClintick was one of five PHS officers
who died from Rocky Mountain Spotted Fever.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.520
A vaccine to combat the disease was ultimately
developed.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.980
One of the most perplexing diseases of the
time was pellagra; 5,000 people a year were

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.600
dying from it in the early years of the century.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.580
PHS physician scientist Joseph Goldberger
carefully studied the disease,

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:35.280
visiting the orphanages and prisons where
pellagra struck most often.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.260
Most doctors believed the disease resulted
from infection.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.760
Convinced of his own theories, Goldberger
and his wife had themselves injected with

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.100
the blood of those who had the disease.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:53.200
His findings were startling; poor diet, not
infection, caused pellagra.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.840
Soon pellagra was conquered by inexpensive
dietary supplements.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:04.780
The Corps pioneered treatment of tuberculosis and bubonic plague control at risk to their own safety.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.360
Officers fought the battles in the laboratories
and in the communities as well.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:15.440
In San Francisco and other cities, the officers worked to vanquish the culprits in bubonic plague,

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.800
rats and ground squirrels and their fleas.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:25.080
Energetic cleanup campaigns over the years
led to the control of the dreaded plague.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:33.480
Venereal disease, particularly at the time
of World War I, was a major concern.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:41.780
[ Music ]

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:47.740
The Service developed tests and public education
campaigns and ran research centers like  this one in Arkansas.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:52.540
Workers took on child health as a responsibility
too.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.100
PHS personnel traveled throughout the countryside
of America

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.320
examining and inoculating youngsters against
diseases such as typhoid.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.540
And then there was the matter of keeping vital
statistics.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.700
Early work in biostatistics kept staffers
busy.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.940
This was the personal computer of the '20s.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:17.320
The compilation and interpretation of statistics
relating to health and disease

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.320
involved the PHS then as now.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:27.000
At the center of PHS work in the '20s and
'30s was disease control and rural sanitation.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.280
Many an officer's attention was occupied with
privies.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:37.820
There were the good ones, the bad ones, and
the worst ones.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:44.160
Along with evaluating privies, the Service
designed, built, and distributed toilets.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:51.300
The bottom line was good outhouses, worthy
of the approval of the Public Health Service,

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:54.600
like this one, bearing the PHS seal.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:02.170
During those years, the Service successfully
battled with dozens of infectious diseases

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:03.889
including malaria, typhus,

00:10:03.889 --> 00:10:06.200
yellow fever, and hookworm.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:12.380
During the '20s and '30s, the Marine Hospitals
remained the core of the Public Health Service.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:17.610
The hospitals employed the majority of PHS
personnel and served as a training ground

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:21.180
for physicians, dentists, and other clinicians.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.840
As the '30s wore on and the nation struggled
its way out of the depression,

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:29.680
the Public Health Service became part of the cure.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:37.569
The Social Security Act of 1935 was landmark
legislation, providing the PHS with the authority

00:10:37.569 --> 00:10:41.920
to make grants to help develop and improve
state and local health departments.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:47.880
[Dr. Parran:] One of the most significant
events in public health that has occurred

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:48.880
in our lifetime...

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:53.509
[Narrator:] The Surgeon General at the time,
Dr. Thomas Parran, was an ardent publicist

00:10:53.509 --> 00:10:55.120
for the health causes of the day.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.320
He made syphilis prevention one of the mainstays
of his mission.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:05.730
His outspokenness on the subject led to more
public attention to venereal disease and its prevention.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:13.340
His conservative predecessor, Surgeon General
Hugh S. Cumming, had served four terms in the position

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:17.420
and generally opposed PHS assistance in local
health matters.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:25.500
In 1936, President Franklin D. Roosevelt relieved
Cumming as Surgeon General

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:29.040
and appointed Parran, the long-time public health officer.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:35.740
The essence of FDR's New Deal resonated with
Parran's considerably broader view of  public health.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:41.680
During the Roosevelt administration, 55 acres
in then-rural Bethesda, Maryland

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.440
became the new home of what had originally
been the Hygienic Laboratory.

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:53.740
[FDR:] The National Institute of Health speaks
the universal language of humanitarianism.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.600
[Narrator:] In 1930, the laboratory's name
had been changed to the National Institute of Health.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:06.080
The move to Bethesda prepared the NIH for
its period of rapid growth in the post-war years.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.320
[FDR:] Recognized no limits.

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:12.260
[Narrator:] 1941 saw the country's entry into
World War II.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:17.460
Public Health Service officers served in several
different branches of the armed forces.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:23.000
Many were assigned to the Coast Guard and
did everything form making sea-borne house

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.320
calls while on convoy patrol, to supporting amphibious landings.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:32.620
Perhaps one of the most fundamental changes
brought about by the war was in nursing.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:37.879
The strain of wear on the country's health
care system made it clear that something

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.860
had to be done to increase the supply of nurses.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.120
The answer was the Cadet Nurse Corps, which
was formed to meet the need.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.420
Women enrolled in nursing schools and received
a free education.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:13:00.020
They were paid a salary by the PHS and were
obligated to perform military or federal service in return for their education.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:09.160
Eight-five percent of the nurses graduated
in the years 1943 to '46 were in the Cadet Nurse Corps.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:14.360
The quality of nursing education was changed
forever.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:21.040
As a result of PHS policy and funding, nursing
schools were no longer in the shadow of hospitals,

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.699
which had previously been their sole sponsors.

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.460
It was a tremendous boost to the profession.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.560
The PHS's most important legacy from World
War II was the Atlanta-based Malaria Control

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:37.640
in War Areas Program, often referred to as the MCWA.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:44.080
Malaria control was a major activity in the
American South and the Caribbean during the war.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:51.460
At the end of the war it became clear that
the MCWA had developed an important role in

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:53.740
infectious disease, research, and control.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:14:01.380
So it was continued, providing practical applications
in public health research techniques to problems

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.400
such as Typhus control.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:09.959
The agency remained at its Atlanta base and
was renamed the Communicable Disease Center

00:14:09.959 --> 00:14:10.959
and later,

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.560
as we know it today, the Centers for Disease
Control and Prevention.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:20.220
With a greatly expanded role, CDC handles
everything from highly toxic viruses

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.900
to quarantine expertise for the space program.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:32.100
Along with the valuable work of the CDC, PHS
dentists like H. Trendley Dean were making

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.400
major contributions to the nation's health.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:40.980
In the 1940s, 95 percent of the population
suffered from tooth decay.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:45.980
But in some parts of the country, people had
low levels of decay,

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.960
though their teeth were mottled and pitted.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:55.440
PHS researchers in the field and the labs
were the prime detectives in solving the case.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:01.800
NIH dentists determined that the teeth were
mottled because of elevated levels of fluoride

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:06.900
in drinking water and that fluoride led to
a reduction in tooth decay.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:13.420
In 1945, Grand Rapids, Michigan was the first
city to test this proposition.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:22.920
At 4 p.m. on January 25th, 1945, Grand Rapids
began adding fluoride to its water supply.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.520
Schoolchildren actively participated.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:28.540
The results were astounding.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.440
Fluoride in the water reduced dental caries
by as much as 60 percent.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.840
Fluoridation became the principal public health
strategy in the prevention of tooth decay.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:45.460
Since the early 1900s, dental and medical
care for Native Americans had been provided

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.060
by PHS personnel on loan to the Indian Field Service.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:55.110
But in 1954, an act of Congress transferred
formal responsibility for the health

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.260
of American Indians to the Public Health Service.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:02.700
It was the hope that a program administered by health professionals could improve

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:06.280
the health of Indians. That proved to be the case.

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:13.880
By 1960, Native American infant mortality
had declined by almost 25 percent,

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:19.020
and the death rate from tuberculosis by almost 50 percent.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:24.720
Today, that program is an agency of the PHS,
the Indian Health Service.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:29.640
Public health physicians also serve the needs
of another,

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:33.640
often forgotten, sector of the population, prison inmates.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:40.700
Since 1930, PHS officers have worked with
the Bureau of Prisons, its facilities and hospitals.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.000
Environmental health issues surfaced in the
'40s.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:52.300
In steel towns like Donora, Pennsylvania,
smog made 6,000 people ill and killed another 120.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:57.580
Along with air pollution, concerns about water
pollution were mounting as well.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:01.320
Radiation in the atmosphere from nuclear testing was apparent.

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:06.500
The PHS began to study radiation and its biological
effects.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:12.080
Environmental health concerns have stayed
on the scene, growing in prominence.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:18.980
Within the CDC, public health teams deal with
toxic substances, and since the '70s,

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:21.980
the National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.640
has dealt with a myriad of industrial and environmental issues.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:30.440
Post-war development in biomedical research
paid rich dividends

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:36.180
and led to Nobel Prize honors for dozens of
investigators supported by NIH grants.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:46.240
Four NIH scientists have been Nobel Laureates:
Marshall Nirenberg for breaking the genetic code.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.500
Julius Axelrod for his work on the central
nervous system,

00:17:51.740 --> 00:17:54.840
Christian Anfinsen won a chemistry prize for
work on amino acids,

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.800
and Carlton Gajdusek for isolating a virus
fatal among natives of New Guinea.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:10.500
As reflected in Dr. Gajdusek's work, international health had become an area of importance for the PHS, one with notable successes.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:17.540
The CDC, for instance, provided leadership
with a global campaign that resulted in the conquest of smallpox.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:24.020
In 1967, Surgeon General William Stewart had
pledged PHS personnel

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.720
to the World Health Organization campaign against smallpox.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:35.419
More than 300 PHS physicians, scientists,
and public health workers, led by the CDC's

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:41.120
Dr. D.A. Henderson, went all over the globe to fight the battle
and they won.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:46.340
By 1977, smallpox had been eradicated throughout
the world.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:52.620
In the 1960s, reorganization brought new programs
to the PHS fold.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:57.730
One of the most significant was the Food and Drug Administration,

00:18:57.730 --> 00:19:01.960
which had been an independent agency since its inception in 1906.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:07.740
Its original responsibility was for the protection
of the American consumer against adulterated

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:10.020
or mislabeled food and drugs.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:17.940
[ Music ]

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:25.520
Today the agency sets standards in the areas
of food, drugs, cosmetics, radiation, health, and medical devices.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:31.180
The agency has labored to expedite and improve
the approval process for new drugs.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:39.300
Reorganization in the early 1970s established
the PHS in its essential form of today.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:46.420
One of those changes was bringing programs
for mental and addictive disorders together into one agency.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:51.940
Today, the Substance Abuse and Mental Health
Services administration administers prevention

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:54.460
and treatment programs in these areas,

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:59.100
while research activities in mental health
and substance abuse are carried out

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.860
by the National Institutes of Health.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:09.400
During the 1970s, the PHS became heavily involved
in the delivery of health services to poor, isolated populations.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:15.620
The Community Health Center Program supported
more than 800 health centers throughout the country

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:21.020
and provided medical care workers to these
communities through the National Health Corps. Service

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:27.940
These programs remain a vital part of the
Public Health Service today as the needs of

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:30.400
the medically underserved continue to grow.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:36.340
The Health Resources and Services Administration
supports both state and community efforts

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.340
to serve those

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:42.340
who are less fortunate and provides health
care practitioners to staff those systems.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:49.360
The organization continues to support the
education of health professionals through

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.360
scholarships and training programs.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.300
To assure the quality and effectiveness of
health services,

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:01.260
the Agency for Health Care Policy and Research has been established.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:06.100
It sponsors health services and medical outcomes research toward the goals

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.220
of improving the practice, organization,

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:11.440
financing, and delivery of health care services.

00:21:14.409 --> 00:21:19.640
The PHS has led the national and global battle
against HIV and AIDS,

00:21:19.649 --> 00:21:24.390
carrying out primary research on the virus
and sponsoring prevention and treatment programs

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:25.840
throughout the country.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.420
All of the agencies of the PHS are engaged
in this monumental public health campaign.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:38.480
The Public Health Service is made up of both
civil service and Commissioned Corps members.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:43.960
In addition to staffing the agencies of the
PHS, the Commissioned Corps provides

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:47.390
clinical and scientific personnel for the Bureau of Prisons,

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:50.860
the Coast Guard, the Environmental Protection Agency,

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:54.300
and the National Oceanographic Atmospheric Administration.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:01.769
In the 1980s, Surgeon General C. Everett Koop
captured the public eye,

00:22:01.769 --> 00:22:06.340
bringing visibility to health issues with
his outspoken reports on AIDS and smoking.

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:12.460
Today, the Public Health Service is part of
the Department of Health and Human Services,

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:16.680
and the heads of its agencies, now called
operating divisions,

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:20.080
report to the Secretary of Health and Human Services.

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:26.720
The Assistant Secretary for Health and the
Surgeon General advise the Secretary on health policy and programs.

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:33.610
The operating divisions of the Public Health
Service provide clinical care while protecting

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:37.660
the consumer through regulation of food, drug,
and medical devices.

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.800
The service also continues to conduct biomedical
and behavioral and health services research

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.560
throughout the United States and around the
world.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:56.660
The PHS maintains its tradition of public
health campaigning with its Healthy People  program

00:22:57.000 --> 00:23:01.080
to promote health awareness and public action
throughout the United States.

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:09.480
And the service continues its scientific and
public education battle against the epidemic of disease caused by tobacco.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:19.900
[ Music ]

00:23:19.909 --> 00:23:24.200
With a wealth of achievements and a proud
history, the Public Health Service

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.700
protects and advances the health of the American people.

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:32.300
It does so with its special blend of science
and government,

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:37.620
tradition and topicality, public service and
personal commitment.

00:23:39.240 --> 00:23:43.720
Its work continues to respond to the ever-changing
mandates of science,

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:47.120
the dictates of government, and the needs
of the people.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:24:08.640
[ Music ]

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.539
This videotape is based on the book Plagues and Politics: The Story of the United States

00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:16.600
Public Health Service, written by Dr. Fitzhugh Mullan.

